  _globals['_ENVIRONMENTSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetEnvironment']._serialized_options = b'\222A\355\005\n\014Environments\022\027Get environment details\032\377\002Retrieves one environment by its Scalekit identifier, including its display name, type, domain and custom domain status. Use this to read the configuration of an environment you already have the id for; call the list endpoint first when you do not. The id must belong to the calling workspace \342\200\224 an environment in another workspace is reported as not found rather than as forbidden.J\235\001\n\003200\022\225\001\n]Returns the environment with its id, display name, type, domain and domain verification state\0224\n2\0320.scalekit.v1.environments.GetEnvironmentResponseJ\\\n\003400\022U\nSThe id is missing, longer than 32 characters, or does not begin with the env prefixJD\n\003404\022=\n;No environment with this id exists in the calling workspace\202\265\030\035\n\031environment_settings:read\030@\212\265\030\230\001\n\017get_environment\022\202\001Get one environment\'s details by id. The id must belong to the caller\'s own workspace \342\200\224 use list_environments to find valid ids.\030\001\202\323\344\223\002\033\022\031/api/v1/environments/{id}'
